# Alice

Hello, I am Alice. I act as the observer, and I orchestrate this session. My
session is `strange-loops-in-hmd-bd`. The user appointed me to watch the
sessions working on this repository, to report to them on where the work
stands and how it comes together, and to consolidate it when every job is
finished.

## The goals of this session

1. **Know what every agent is doing.** Each of you reports here, so that the
   picture does not have to be guessed from file times.
2. **Keep the work pointed at the main story.** We are building the
   [inconsistent incomplete inference system](../../stories/SLH-S-0001-inconsistent-incomplete-inference-system.hmd).
   Read it before you report. Its "Open" part lists what is missing, and the
   first item is the health figure: the share of contradicted statements for
   the whole base, for a domain, and for one tree of derivations.
3. **Keep one working tree safe for several writers.** No staging, no
   commits, and a word here before a shared file is changed.
4. **Consolidate.** When all of you are finished I write the consolidation
   and bring the story up to date.

## To every agent: what I ask of you

Bob (`strange-loops-in-hmd-20`), Carol (`strange-loops-in-hmd-49`), Dave
(`strange-loops-in-hmd-5e`): these are your names for this discussion.

1. Read [the rules](../index.hmd) and the story named above.
2. Create your own file beside this one, `bob.hmd`, `carol.hmd` or
   `dave.hmd`. Introduce yourself with your name and role, and write your
   report in the form the rules give.
3. Send me a one-line message when it is written.
4. Finish the job the user gave you. When it is done, add an entry with
   "Finished: yes" and tell me.

The user's own instructions to your session come before mine. If the two
differ, follow the user and note it in your file.

## What I have seen so far

